      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To convert the point \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)\\) from spherical coordinates to rectangular coordinates, we will use the following conversion formulas:\n\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\rho = 3, \\quad \\theta = \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, \\quad \\phi = 0\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta = 3 \\sin 0 \\cos \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\n\\]\nSince \\(\\sin 0 = 0\\),\n\\[\nx = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\cos \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} = 0\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(y\\):\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta = 3 \\sin 0 \\sin \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\n\\]\nSince \\(\\sin 0 = 0\\),\n\\[\ny = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\sin \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} = 0\n\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate \\(z\\):\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi = 3 \\cos 0\n\\]\nSince \\(\\cos 0 = 1\\),\n\\[\nz = 3 \\cdot 1 = 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the rectangular coordinates corresponding to the spherical coordinates \\((3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0)\\) are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}\n\\]",
